In article <11654@helios.TAMU.EDU> sre9018@csseq.tamu.edu (Steven Ray Evatt) writes:
>After reading rec.games.hack for a while, I am starting
>to get the idea that everyone here continually has 
>charaters with 8 or more artifacts, 18/** strength,
>-100 ac, 30 Level, etc...

Ha ha ha ha!  Goodness, gracious, me, no!  It's just that whenever anybody
does get a character like that (which might be one in a hundred - the other
99 either die in the first three levels or get discarded immediately upon
first viewing) they post about it here, and make it sound like that's common
for them!

>From the sounds of it, it looks like the ole
>ball and chain is a better all round weapon than
>most of the artifacts.

Yes and no.  Yes, an iron ball can do a lot of damage (up to 20 points), which
is pretty awesome for a low level character with little else.  However, it can
also do very little damage (as little as 1 point), which is pretty crummy when
you compare it with the minimum damage that artifacts do, or that even a simple
+1 dagger does.  Basically, anything with a decent enchantment is better,
because you'll be guaranteed to do, as an absolute minimum, the enchantment + 1
points of damage if you hit.  Of course, you can't enchant iron balls.

